.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt GH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm gh
.Nd GitHub's command-line program
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar subcommand
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
works with GitHub from the shell: repositories, issues, pull requests,
releases, Actions runs, projects and the REST and GraphQL interfaces.
.Ql gh help
lists its commands, and
.Ql gh help Ar command
or
.Ql gh Ar command Fl -help
describes one.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root has
.Nm
when it is built with the agents layer:
.Ql make ARCH=x86_64 GNU_AGENTS=gh os-real-gnu-ext2 ,
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all ,
which the release to the installed machine uses.
The program is GitHub's own build of version 2.102.0, a static Go
executable, installed unmodified as the release has it.
.Pa /opt/gh/bin/gh
is the program, and
.Pa /usr/bin/gh
and
.Pa /bin/gh
link to it.
GitHub's license, MIT, is
.Pa /opt/gh/LICENSE .
The release's own manual pages are in
.Pa /opt/gh/share/man/man1 ;
.Xr man 1
does not read them, and
.Ql gh help
has the same text.
.Ss Signing in over SSH
.Ql gh auth login
asks for the host, the protocol Git is to use, HTTPS or SSH, and a way to
sign in.
With
.Dq Login with a web browser ,
.Nm
prints a one-time code and the address
.Lk https://github.com/login/device .
The machine has no web browser for
.Nm
to open, so open that address on any other computer, sign in to GitHub
there and enter the code;
.Nm
waits for GitHub's answer and then stores the token it is given.
.Pp
Instead,
.Ql gh auth login --with-token
reads a personal access token from standard input, and a token in the
environment variable
.Ev GH_TOKEN
is used without signing in and is not stored.
.Ql gh auth status
says which account is signed in and where its token is kept.
.Ql gh auth setup-git
makes
.Xr git 1
ask
.Nm
for the credentials of a GitHub host, so that a clone or push over HTTPS
needs no other sign-in.
.Ss Where the token lives
.Nm
keeps a token in the system's credential store, the Secret Service of the
D-Bus session bus, where there is one, and otherwise in plain text.
Rach2 runs no Secret Service, so the token is written to
.Pa ~/.config/gh/hosts.yml ,
with mode 0600, beside the settings in
.Pa ~/.config/gh/config.yml .
.Ev GH_CONFIG_DIR ,
or
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
followed by
.Pa /gh ,
names another directory.
.Ql gh auth logout
removes the token.
.Ss Updates and telemetry
.Nm
does not replace itself; a new version comes with a new build of the root.
On a terminal it asks GitHub once a day whether a newer release exists and
prints a notice when one does, which
.Ev GH_NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER
set to any value turns off.
It sends GitHub usage telemetry unless
.Ql gh config set telemetry disabled
or
.Ev GH_TELEMETRY Ns =false
turns it off.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /opt/gh/bin/gh
the program
.It Pa /opt/gh/LICENSE
its license
.It Pa ~/.config/gh/hosts.yml
the hosts signed in to, with their tokens
.It Pa ~/.config/gh/config.yml
the settings
.It Pa ~/.local/state/gh
the state of the update check and a device identifier
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error, 2 when a command is cancelled, and 4 when a
command needs a sign-in that has not been made.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sign in, then list the open issues of a repository:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gh auth login
$ gh issue list --repo toksaitov/rach2
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1
.Pp
.Lk https://cli.github.com/manual "The GitHub CLI manual"
